<urn:atm:triage:finding/AM-PHASEEND2-PLANDOC-STALE-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AM-PHASEEND2-PLANDOC-STALE-001" ;
  triage:title "docs/project-plan.md still tags Phase AL and Phase AM sections '[PLAN HARDENING]' even though both phases' own plan documents now carry status: complete frontmatter" ;
  triage:description "docs/project-plan.md's section headers for '## 43. Phase AL — Build the Minimal Tokio HTTP Runtime' and '## 44. Phase AM — Deletion-Only Transport Cleanup' both still carry the '[PLAN HARDENING]' tag, which reads as still-in-planning. This contradicts docs/plans/phase-al/plan-phase-al.md and docs/plans/phase-am/plan-phase-am.md, whose frontmatter both now set status: complete (the latter fixed earlier this phase under AM-END-PLAN-DOC-FRONTMATTER-STALE, which only touched the per-phase plan docs' own frontmatter, not project-plan.md's section headers). project-plan.md is a mandatory baseline source per the QA workflow's acceptance-gate step, so this is a real internal inconsistency between two authoritative planning documents, not a cosmetic nit. Surfaced by req-qa during QA-AM-PHASEEND-2 (second Phase AM phase-ending review) and independently confirmed via direct grep against integrate/phase-am@96299ad8." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-am" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "doc-consistency" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "single-branch" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-12T06:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "Fixed by arch-ctm's FIX-AL9-AM-RECONCILIATION-1 (docs/al9-am-evidence-reconciliation PR #861, commit 4c0c1d68). docs/project-plan.md sections 43 and 44 both changed from [PLAN HARDENING] to [COMPLETE]. Independently re-confirmed by 4 reviewers this round (req-qa, arch-qa, ruthless-boundary-qa, and quality-mgr's own grep) at commit 2cdedd4d; no remaining [PLAN HARDENING] tags in the document." ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
